            "result_text": "I've created a complete git server setup with automatic web deployment. Here's what you have:\n\n## Files Created:\n\n1. **SETUP_INSTRUCTIONS.md** — Complete step-by-step guide to set up on your server\n2. **setup-git-server.sh** — Automated script to initialize the git repo\n3. **setup-nginx.sh** — Automated script to install/configure nginx\n4. **nginx.conf** — Web server configuration for port 8080\n5. **post-receive-hook.sh** — The deployment hook (reference)\n6. **local-demo.sh** — Test the setup locally on your computer\n\n## Quick Summary:\n\nThe setup creates:\n- **Git repository** at `/git/server` (bare, so you can push to it)\n- **Web root** at `/var/www/html` (served by nginx on port 8080)\n- **Post-receive hook** that auto-deploys on each push\n\nWhen you `git push`, the hook automatically:\n1. Clones the pushed code to a temp directory\n2. Copies files to `/var/www/html`\n3. Sets proper permissions\n\nThen `curl http://server:8080/hello.html` serves those files.\n\n## To Test Locally First:\n\n```bash\nbash /app/local-demo.sh\ncd /tmp/git-deploy-demo/work\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\ncat /tmp/git-deploy-demo/www/hello.html  # Should show: hello world\n```\n\nFollow **SETUP_INSTRUCTIONS.md** to deploy this on your actual server."
